2026-09-27T09:51:05.0289360Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0289895Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0290400Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0291213Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0292048Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0292175Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0292402Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0292711Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0292970Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0293392Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0293723Z ================
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0293969Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0294272Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0294869Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0295205Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0295377Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0295816Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0296101Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0296345Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0296999Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0297615Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0298762Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0299691Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0299882Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0300666Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0301630Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0302078Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0302564Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0303540Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0303688Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0304003Z ========
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0304187Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0306393Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0308737Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0309122Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0383447Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0384877Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0386175Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0387137Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0387848Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0388623Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0388800Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0389197Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0389426Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0391260Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0393558Z 
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0394723Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0396287Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:51:05.0396676Z 
